WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.346
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.770
SPEAKER: Wedding cakes
have become bigger and more

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.640
elaborate over the years.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.610
Today's wedding
cakes are multitiered

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:14.380
and even multiflavored.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:16.630
They're typically
covered in fondant icing

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.330
and decorated with
ornate sugar flowers.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.790
The finished product is
an edible work of art,

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.380
perfect for that special day.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.320
These customized wedding
cakes are covered in fondant.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.170
The specializing
acts as a canvas

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.375
on which delicious
designs can be created.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.470
The baker starts
by making chocolate

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.510
cakes for the bottom tier.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:44.730
Once the cakes come
out of the oven,

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:48.000
she transfers them
directly to the fridge.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.895
The cool, firm cakes are
easy to slice into layers.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.890
She spreads buttercream
frosting between the layers.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:01:00.470
The frosting ingredients include
lightly salted butter, icing

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:03.650
sugar, and Dutch cocoa powder.

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:07.070
Layer by layer, she builds the
tier to the desired height.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:12.020
She puts the tier
back in the fridge.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.880
While it's
solidifying, she makes

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.730
the gum paste that will be used
to craft the edible flowers.

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:21.660
First, she adds icing
sugar to egg whites.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.500
Then thins out the mixture
with a teaspoon of water.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.120
Next, she adds food coloring.

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.870
She mixes the ingredients
for a couple of minutes

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.400
until they're
thoroughly blended.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.550
She adds tylose powder, a
synthetic version of gum Arabic

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:46.465
to harden the mixture.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.660
After another 15
seconds of mixing,

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.580
the gum paste is
ready for kneading.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.000
The baker rubs some
vegetable shortening

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.560
on her hands for lubrication.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.460
She sprinkles some icing
sugar on the table to prevent

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.620
the gum paste from sticking.

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.730
Then she kneads the gum
paste for 5 to 10 minutes.

00:02:08.199 --> 00:02:09.645
Now, the artistry begins.

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:13.110
She uses a set of
modeling tools made

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.760
of food-safe, nonstick plastic.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.140
First, she makes a little hat
out of the pink gum paste,

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:23.890
then she rolls out another
piece until it's paper thin.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:26.170
The baker uses a gum
paste cutter to cut

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.640
out several teardrop shapes.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:31.630
One at a time, she
lays the teardrops

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.790
out on a hard foam mat.

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.010
She thins and curls
the edges with a ball

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.490
tipped modeling tool to create
a natural-looking rose petal.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:44.130
Then she switches
to a scribe tool.

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:47.550
She curls back the edges to make
the petal even more lifelike.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.680
Then she applies
tasteless edible glue.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.520
She adheres the first
petal along to the point

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:00.230
of the gum paste hat.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:02.180
She wraps it all the
way around to create

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.250
the center of the rose.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:06.410
The baker attaches
the next layer,

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.690
this time using two petals.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:10.610
She adds several
additional layers

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:15.380
using two more petals each time
until the rose is complete.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.720
She snips off the
base of the hat,

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:20.090
then lets the glue
dry for 15 minutes.

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.560
The baker uses green gum
paste to make the leaves.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.500
She rolls the paste thicker
at the base and thinner

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:30.820
at the top.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:33.760
Then she presses the sheet
against the top of the board

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.090
to produce vertical veins.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.200
She centers her leaf shape
cutter over one of the veins

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.250
and cuts out a leaf.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.180
After attaching a
wire to the base,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.580
she uses a silicone
stamp to imprint

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.650
smaller veins on the leaf.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:54.390
This makes it look
more realistic.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:01.640
The baker curls the leaf's
edges with a round tool.

00:04:04.220 --> 00:04:06.890
She uses a different tool to
deepen some of the veining

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.120
and complete the leaf.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:13.240
The baker sets her decorations
aside and removes the cake

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:14.710
tiers from the refrigerator.

00:04:16.209 --> 00:04:18.725
She firmly applies the fondant
over the chilled chocolate

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:19.525
frosting.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:25.890
She made the fondant earlier
with melted marshmallows,

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:30.360
butter, icing, sugar, vanilla
extract, and food coloring.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.820
She applies fondant to
the remaining tiers,

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:33.900
then stacks them.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:40.010
She begins decorating this cake
with ribbon and Italian lace.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.750
She attaches the flowers
with stiff edible glue

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:49.040
made from egg whites, icing,
sugar, and lemon juice.

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:51.650
She can also make
edible ribbons and lace

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:55.460
by pouring liquid gum paste
into the appropriate molds.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.030
This special gum paste uses
corn syrup and cornstarch

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.580
to reach the right consistency.

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:04.490
A magnificent custom-made
cake is designed

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:09.110
to be a showpiece at the wedding
reception-- admired, devoured,

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.220
and always remembered.

